-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- PEDAGOGICAL INTELLIGENCE — the record, mostly empty on purpose
--
-- Seventeen fields per teaching lesson. Three are derived from the
-- curriculum as it stands. Fourteen are what a teacher learns by
-- teaching, and this College has taught nobody, so they are marked
-- not_yet_evidenced and carry no value.
--
-- That emptiness is the point. A pedagogy record filled with plausible
-- prose about misconceptions nobody has observed would be the most
-- damaging kind of invention in this project: it would look like
-- classroom knowledge and would be guesswork, and every future edition
-- would inherit it as fact. 114 lessons x 17 fields =
-- 1938 rows, of which 342 carry evidence.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────






